From 398017ce0f5c5854eb6253da6a97fe87d66129fb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LHBUSA <sales@localhomebuyersusa.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 19:52:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(dna): rank the eligible fighter population, not a UUID
 window (#27)

/v1/ufc/dna/query scanned at most 1000 rows of the 26,167-row snapshot history
ordered by fighter UUID, resolved "latest snapshot" inside that window, then
ranked and limited. For the default broad query the window covered 122 of the
3161 fighters that have a snapshot, so the published top-50 was the top-50 of an
arbitrary UUID prefix and meta.truncated was true on almost every call.

Ranking now happens in one stable SQL function, public.ufc_dna_metric_ranking:
resolve each fighter's latest eligible row first, then filter, then rank the
whole matched population, then limit.

Deliberately unchanged: as_of resolution (latest row <= as_of, chosen without
regard to the metric filters, so an older passing row never stands in for a
newer failing one); the confidence gate and its 'low' default; min/max against
the stored numeric value; explicit nulls stay null and sort last in BOTH
directions; the name-then-id tie-break; every parameter, field name, type and
row shape.

Deliberately changed, and documented as such: meta.candidates and
meta.candidates_total are now both the eligible population that was ranked (one
latest snapshot or stance split per fighter) and are always equal;
meta.truncated is always false because no scan cap remains. The keys are kept so
existing clients do not break.

Proven before shipping, on a local PG17 copy of production (26,167 snapshots,
3,177 fighters, 44,147 stance splits):
- equivalence: 154/154 cases identical to a line-for-line port of the current
  Worker algorithm with the 1000-row cap removed. Zero mismatches, zero
  tie-order differences.
- plan: index-only scan on ufc_fighter_dna_snapshots_latest_idx resolves the
  3,161 latest snapshots, the window stops at rank <= limit. ~70 ms warm for the
  broad default (~80 ms at min_confidence=insufficient&limit=200, ~45 ms for a
  stance query), against ~487 ms p50 for the current two-round-trip path.
- new regression tests build a 1,200-fighter population whose best values sit
  entirely outside the old 1000-row window and assert the true top-50 is
  returned, that ranking precedes the limit, that active filtering precedes
  ranking, that superseded rows never stand in, and that an explicit null is
  matched, sorts last in both directions and satisfies no bound.

Not deployed. The migration is not applied and the Worker is not released;
API_VERSION and the OpenAPI version are staged at 2026-09-12.1 so the release
metadata is not stale when it is. Rollback is a file, and it is ordered: roll
the Worker back first, then drop the function, because a missing PostgREST
function reads as a missing schema (503 dna_not_available).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PzDoDm2gk69cHQbhCQruBG
